*   Topic: Password recovery (specifically when manual fallback helps).
    *   Format: Substack Note.
    *   Word count: 60-100 words.
    *   Style: Plain text, one or two short paragraphs, no hashtags, no title.

    *   Automated recovery (email/SMS) is standard but fails.
    *   Failure cases: lost access to email, hacked phone numbers, de-activated accounts.
    *   Manual fallback (human review, ID verification) ensures the user isn't permanently locked out forever.
    *   Importance of balancing security vs. accessibility.

    Automated password recovery systems are great until they aren't. If you lose access to both your email and your phone number, standard workflows hit a dead end. This is where a manual fallback becomes essential. A process involving human review or document-based identity verification ensures that legitimate users aren't permanently locked out of their digital lives. For high-stakes accounts, manual intervention provides a safety net that algorithms alone simply cannot offer.

